  I saw a few messages regarding running nethack as a BBS door and
saw some people were having trouble so I thought I'd post how I do it.
  First of all, to stop users from having the SHELL '!' command.  
You dont have to change the source code and recompile it, the
simplest way (by the way, I run it on an IBM - doesnt matter what
BBS type though) is to use a hex editor and edit NETHACK.EXE, change
all COMSPEC references in there to something else, then before
running nethack set the new environment variable to something else.
  At one time I set it to run something to add the users name
to a 'bad users' list but later I wrote a pager and when the
user hit '!' it would page the Sysop and go into a chat mode.

Example of a batch file:
set NUSHELL=PAGER.EXE
nethack
 
  Now the other problem is users either hanging up or getting hung
up while in nethack.  You'll have to also load up a carrier detect
program beforehand.  I use WatchDog.  Itll reboot the system (and
hence the board).   So you have to install that before running
nethack and remove after.
  Then I *believe* (I cant remember if it was necessary) I used
x00, installing it before and removing it after.  That is necessary
to send/receive info through the com port.
  
  The other thing I use is a file to create various bulletins and
score files (that I wrote).  For example, top killer, top score
for each class.  top score for each player...
  Then I also wrote a door manager.  It keeps track of each players
options, number of times played that day - only allows the user in
the door if he has more than 20 minutes remaning, lets him
view scores, pick pet names, his class, etc.   Then before running
the batch file, it writes out a proper NETHACK.CNF file with all
the appropriate info.
  Note it doesnt matter what BBS you are using
  The only thing I dont have is a time limit.  A user can go in
the door indefinitely (but you'll kind of KNOW hes been in there
since the BBS as well as the door keeps a log).  Doorway would
fix that problem (as well as the shelling problem).  I had run
into memory problems with Doorway though, but if you can get
it running it should be enough.  Dont have to worry about watchdog
or x00, or shelling, or time...
 
  have fun!



